    "content": "Work that focuses on LLM planning often reports low success rates and provides high-level analysesof why models fail—for example, prompt-sensitive pattern-matching and the need for planner-basedrepair [27]. Other recent evaluations include cost/efficiency comparisons with some failure-modebreakdowns [6, 28], but they do not typically emphasize fine-grained analyses of how failuresunfold. Furthermore, few studies examine variable levels of feedback, and we are aware of nonethat systematically combine modern prompting techniques with feedback on a planning task like the8-puzzle to analyze how these factors modulate performance and failure types, leaving the effects ofprompting and feedback on such tasks under-examined.",
